Specifically, the request details for the following Ukrainian state sources were
ported from that project's Python scripts into TypeScript:

  - reyestr.court.gov.ua (ЄДРСР)          from skills/ukrainian-court-practice/scripts/edrsr.py
  - lpd(-api-prod).court.gov.ua (ЛПД ВС)  from skills/ukrainian-court-practice/scripts/lpd.py
  - zakon.rada.gov.ua name resolver       from skills/ukrainian-legislation/scripts/rada.py

Their measured behaviour of those endpoints — the POST-only ЄДРСР search, the
inlined CAPTCHA modal, the per-host User-Agent requirements, the query grammar
traps — is the reason those modules are written the way they are. Attribution is
also kept inline in the source files that carry ported logic.

---

Legislation texts and document metadata in mcp/ua-legal-sources/test/fixtures/
are open data published by the Verkhovna Rada of Ukraine open data portal
(https://data.rada.gov.ua), used under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International (CC BY 4.0). They are excerpts, retained verbatim so that parser
tests run against the registry's real output rather than an idealised copy.

  Source: Верховна Рада України, Портал відкритих даних, https://data.rada.gov.ua
  Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

No court decisions and no personal data from ЄДРСР are included in this
repository. The ЄДРСР test fixtures are written by hand.
